Local fix (not upstream): force the GSP-reported PCIe peer caps for CMP cards.

Anchored with no surrounding context on purpose. The two assignment lines below
are unique in gpu.c, while the lines around them are not stable across the
supported drivers: 610.x closes _gpuInitPcieP2PCapability() immediately after
them, whereas 615.71.09 adds

    pGpu->bPcieP2PSkipChipsetCheck = p2pCapsParams.bSkipChipsetCheck;

before the closing brace. Carrying trailing context here made the hunk apply to
one driver generation and fail on the other; matching only the replaced lines
applies cleanly (fuzz 0) to every version in driver/VERSION.


--- a/src/nvidia/src/kernel/gpu/gpu.c
+++ b/src/nvidia/src/kernel/gpu/gpu.c
@@ -2518,2 +2518,18 @@ _gpuInitPcieP2PCapability
-    pGpu->pcieP2PReadCaps = p2pCapsParams.p2pReadCapsStatus;
-    pGpu->pcieP2PWriteCaps = p2pCapsParams.p2pWriteCapsStatus;
+    pGpu->pcieP2PReadCaps = p2pCapsParams.p2pReadCapsStatus;
+    pGpu->pcieP2PWriteCaps = p2pCapsParams.p2pWriteCapsStatus;
+
+    // CMP 170HX/220HX GSP firmware reports PCIe peer access as unsupported
+    // even when the host topology and BAR1 path can carry it. This patch is
+    // applied only for an explicit --p2p build; keep every other device and
+    // the default build on the firmware-reported values.
+    {
+        NvU32 cmpDevId = pGpu->idInfo.PCIDeviceID >> 16;
+        if ((cmpDevId == 0x20C2) || (cmpDevId == 0x2082))
+        {
+            pGpu->pcieP2PReadCaps = 0;
+            pGpu->pcieP2PWriteCaps = 0;
+            NV_PRINTF(LEVEL_ERROR,
+                      "CMPUNLOCK_P2P: GSP PCIe peer caps forced to OK (devId=0x%x)\n",
+                      cmpDevId);
+        }
+    }
